 $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=2-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ | $-7$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-7$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](images/5c/5cd074670c05cea0c68db75c7e1a57309c017c97556e976f2db4c3bf1b358a85.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Curve Defined Parametrically"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087722 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087523 :question/id #uuid "a792fa16-e1fd-5f30-a128-bbc49a285429" :question/math-academy-id "e-5099" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t^2-6t, \\,\\,\\, y=t^4+4, \\quad t \\in (-\\infty , \\infty),\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2}-6t \\\\  & ={(t-3)}^{2}-(3)^{2} \\\\  & ={(t-3)}^{2}-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\left( t-3\\right)^2 \\geq 0,$ we can conclude that $x \\geq -9.$\n\n- To find the range of $y=t^4+4,$ notice that $t^4 \\geq 0,$ and consequently $y \\geq 4.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $x \\geq -9$ and $y \\geq 4.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbf0ad0-a7c5-5c0f-a06c-9210fdc244ef" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b66d32e-948b-514c-b79f-7024a2f95a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge 0, y \\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084915} {:answer/id #uuid "da35ba7d-f113-5b40-a7a6-b2c42bd62346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le 9, y \\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084916} {:answer/id #uuid "258a9d84-41a0-5795-96ec-43227eb669e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge - 9, y \\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084917} {:answer/id #uuid "5ebf0762-ff4f-5c76-b927-68997ac64c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge 3, y \\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084918} {:answer/id #uuid "79d27931-8421-5bf6-ada7-8e1092bed54c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le 3, y \\le 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084919}] :answer-field/id #uuid "18ecd093-d7cd-5c78-b7bd-6c08932d88af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084914}] :question/id #uuid "cffccf04-c19e-5fb5-b78b-fad25744a2e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-16203" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n$x = t^{2} + 6t, y = \\sqrt{t}, t \\ge 0$,\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "826fa152-dc36-549b-9605-6469987effb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084921} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa56dbb-4bdc-595b-a52e-206b82d037f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084922} {:answer/id #uuid "08b41fba-1724-5283-bf6f-b6085984f640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084923} {:answer/id #uuid "54b078f0-45a8-55da-af62-219d9e82ff7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x > 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084924} {:answer/id #uuid "78cddf61-66f0-5dd7-acbe-c9eb4b6a1bd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084925}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f4214e40-b614-5435-bc11-5fb80952a34c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084920}] :question/id #uuid "105e48e2-d41e-5a20-8724-87cae30a3d12" :question/math-academy-id "q-16205" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n$x = t^{2} - 4t, y = t^{2}, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)$,\ndetermine the range of $x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26795cb5-46f0-593d-bbbf-be3f06b14875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -4,\\,y\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275826} {:answer/id #uuid "324e6b9f-c15b-5458-9243-fbb2407d28b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,y\\le -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275921} {:answer/id #uuid "a0fae690-6db1-517e-a307-69dfa66a5f91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -\\frac{1}{2},\\,y\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276927} {:answer/id #uuid "b1310550-084d-5243-93a9-5a121ec3fd09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -\\frac{1}{4},\\,y\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277063} {:answer/id #uuid "b4cbc30c-7bf6-5ea9-9861-98cf564bf084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{1}{4},\\,y\\le -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1310550-084d-5243-93a9-5a121ec3fd09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -\\frac{1}{4},\\,y\\ge -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277063} :answer-field/id #uuid "adfdb777-9023-51f2-b4b7-4925f3b6bdcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278027}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c5d5a76-6d19-5d2e-8ac8-15cac8c3ca23" :question/math-academy-id "q-16149" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}+t,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-2,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2}+t \\\\  & ={(t+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & ={(t+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${(t+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\ge 0,$ we can conclude that $x\\ge -\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that ${t}^{2}\\ge 0.$ Therefore, we can conclude that $y\\ge -2.$\n\nSo, the ranges are $x\\ge -\\frac{1}{4}$ and $y\\ge -2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234355 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d3103a8-b551-5ab8-b607-7a72a3223b84" :question/math-academy-id "q-73604" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}-2t-1,\\,\\,\\,y=\\sqrt{t}-4,\\,t\\ge 0,\n$$\n\ndetermine the range of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2}-2t-1 \\\\  & ={(t-1)}^{2}-{1}^{2}-1 \\\\  & ={(t-1)}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${(t-1)}^{2}\\ge 0,$ we can conclude that $x\\ge -2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259556 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a77d04e-330f-5969-a265-1f92418525cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257159} {:answer/id #uuid "626a5119-9348-5540-b3a7-b85b3ca60c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257650} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1a232f-2d58-5284-b6e0-3cf1d3a00e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257995} {:answer/id #uuid "d5e8ee6a-3d7f-59d7-ace8-98f88ea43ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258658} {:answer/id #uuid "fd04b0fd-3ef4-5e4e-b82d-fabc59df44b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "626a5119-9348-5540-b3a7-b85b3ca60c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257650} :answer-field/id #uuid "c11d5b8b-fe59-57a7-8e6b-14dd5adaef71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259369}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2de12943-54f8-500d-9e95-bde9a205cbca" :question/math-academy-id "q-123763" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\sqrt{t+9},\\,\\,\\,y=t+1,\\,t\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the range of $x,$ note that $\\sqrt{t+9}\\ge 3$ for all $t\\ge 0.$ Consequently, $x=2\\sqrt{t+9}\\ge 6.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude that $x\\ge 6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259557 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fc92ce1-7d99-535d-8470-6bc513682293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257039} {:answer/id #uuid "2a2e93ef-86d7-5dbc-848f-aca59b976bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257154} {:answer/id #uuid "7eda883f-3d24-5b1c-b928-523fd6537cd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257912} {:answer/id #uuid "8dcfa983-5ef3-5c2e-9c9a-f6886ae38ec3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258029} {:answer/id #uuid "de9f47c6-7fdd-57a8-bdac-638af6b59ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7eda883f-3d24-5b1c-b928-523fd6537cd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257912} :answer-field/id #uuid "01f4ba3a-bccf-5208-8e4a-9fe56858