swer/id #uuid "69ec357b-1fff-5c11-ae8a-d1015ea3e5ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300494} :answer-field/id #uuid "f07a0108-c4ed-546b-a41a-5190fbafa2bc" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301993}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "400ebb98-16e3-549a-88aa-0bf9b1800aca" :question/math-academy-id "q-327866" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\le $\n{{field-3}}.\n\n \n\nThe range of $y$ is \n{{field-4}}{{field-5}}\n$y\\le $\n{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have \n$-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2} & \\le -\\frac{9}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2} & \\le x\\le \\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{9}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{9}{2}.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have \n$-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3} & \\le \\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3} & \\le y\\le \\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{5}{3}\\le y\\le \\frac{5}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d30f18