 #edb/ref 17592186302004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dc80a819-3c24-5625-baac-562a70097b16" :question/math-academy-id "q-327880" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=-\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\le $\n{{field-3}}.\n\nThe range of $y$ is \n{{field-4}}\n$\\le y$\n{{field-5}}{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -4 & \\le 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 4 \\\\ -4+1 & \\le 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1\\le 4+1 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-3\\le x\\le 5.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ \nwe have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{2} & \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} & \\le -\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{2} & \\le y\\le \\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-\\frac{7}{2}\\le y\\le \\frac{7}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e53605c5-4363-5d5f-b627-9bba58dd0c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{29}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e53605c5-4363-5d5f-b627-9bba58dd0c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{29}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301099} :answer-field/i